4 "// If we got a handshake failure when resuming a session, throw away"] [258 4 "// the session ticket. See RFC 5077, Section 3.2."] [259 4 "//"] [260 4 "// RFC 8446 makes no mention of dropping tickets on failure, but it"] [261 4 "// does require servers to abort on invalid binders, so we need to"] [262 4 "// delete tickets to recover from a corrupted PSK."] [272 3 "// Split hello into inner and outer"] [275 3 "// Overwrite the server name in the outer hello with the public facing"] [276 3 "// name."] [278 3 "// Generate a new random for the outer hello."] [285 3 "// NOTE: we don't do PSK GREASE, in line with boringssl, it's meant to"] [286 3 "// work around _possibly_ broken middleboxes, but there is little-to-no"] [287 3 "// evidence that this is actually a problem."] [314 2 "// serverHelloMsg is not included in the transcript"] [330 2 "// If we are negotiating a protocol version that's lower than what we"] [331 2 "// support, check for the server downgrade canaries."] [332 2 "// See RFC 8446, Section 4.1.3."] [357 45 "// arbace: not a TLS 1.2 session"] [370 1 "// fips140ems is a GODEBUG variable that can be set to 0 to disable the"] [371 1 "// enforcement of Extended Master Secret in FIPS 140-3 mode."] [382 2 "// ticketSupported is a TLS 1.2 extension (as TLS 1.3 replaced tickets with PSK"] [383 2 "// identities) and ECH requires and forces TLS 1.3."] [387 3 "// Require DHE on resumption as it guarantees forward secrecy against"] [388 3 "// compromise of the session ticket key. See RFC 8446, Section 4.2.9."] [392 2 "// Session resumption is not allowed if renegotiating because"] [393 2 "// renegotiation is primarily used to allow a client to send a client"] [394 2 "// certificate, which would be skipped if session resumption occurred."] [399 2 "// Try to resume a previously negotiated TLS session, if available."] [410 3 "// arbace: a session of a PSK handshake has no certificate to check."] [414 2 "// Check that version used for the previous session is still valid."] [427 3 "// Expired certificate, delete the entry."] [433 4 "// The original connection had InsecureSkipVerify, while this doesn't."] [437 4 "// This should be ensured by the cache key, but protect the"] [438 4 "// application from a faulty ClientSessionCache implementation."] [447 4 "// No valid chains, delete the entry."] [454 3 "// In TLS 1.2 the cipher suite must match the resumed session. Ensure we"] [455 3 "// are still offering it."] [460 3 "// FIPS 140-3 requires the use of Extended Master Secret."] [472 2 "// Check that the session ticket is not expired."] [478 2 "// In TLS 1.3 the KDF hash must match the resumed session. Ensure we"] [479 2 "// offer at least one cipher suite with that hash."] [501 3 "// For 0-RTT, the cipher suite has to match exactly, and we need to be"] [502 3 "// offering the same ALPN."] [513 2 "// Set the pre_shared_key extension. See RFC 8446, Section 4.2.11.1."] [522 2 "// Compute the PSK binders. See RFC 8446, Section 4.2.11.2."] [553 1 "// Does the handshake, either a full one or resumes old session. Requires hs.c,"] [554 1 "// hs.hello, hs.serverHello, and, optionally, hs.session to be set."] [558 2 "// If we did not load a session (hs.session == nil), but we did set a"] [559 2 "// session ID in the transmitted client hello (hs.hello.sessionId != nil),"] [560 2 "// it means we tried to negotiate TLS 1.3 and sent a random session ID as a"] [561 2 "// compatibility measure (see RFC 8446, Section 4.1.2)."] [562 2 "//"] [563 2 "// Since we're now handshaking for TLS 1.2, if the server echoed the"] [564 2 "// transmitted ID back to us, we know mischief is afoot: the session ID"] [565 2 "// was random and can't possibly be recognized by the server."] [578 2 "// No signatures of the handshake are needed in a resumption."] [579 2 "// Otherwise, in a full handshake, if we don't have any certificates"] [580 2 "// configured then we will never send a CertificateVerify message and"] [581 2 "// thus no signatures are needed in that case