uded in the transcript, but not until after we"] [1018 2 "// check the client version, since the state before this message was"] [1019 2 "// sent is used during verification."] [1106 1 "// defaultMaxRSAKeySize is the maximum RSA key size in bits that we are willing"] [1107 1 "// to verify the signatures of during a TLS handshake."] [1124 1 "// verifyServerCertificate parses and verifies the provided chain, setting"] [1125 1 "// c.verifiedChains and c.peerCertificates or sending the appropriate alert."] [1187 39 "// arbace"] [1214 36 "// arbace"] [1221 36 "// arbace"] [1229 1 "// certificateRequestInfoFromMsg generates a CertificateRequestInfo from a TLS"] [1230 1 "// <= 1.2 CertificateRequest, making an effort to fill in missing information."] [1249 3 "// Prior to TLS 1.2, signature schemes did not exist. In this case we"] [1250 3 "// make up a list based on the acceptable certificate types, to help"] [1251 3 "// GetClientCertificate and SupportsCertificate select the right certificate."] [1252 3 "// The hash part of the SignatureScheme is a lie here, because"] [1253 3 "// TLS 1.0 and 1.1 always use MD5+SHA1 for RSA and SHA1 for ECDSA."] [1272 2 "// Filter the signature schemes based on the certificate types."] [1273 2 "// See RFC 5246, Section 7.4.4 (where it calls this \"somewhat complicated\")."] [1307 2 "// No acceptable certificate found. Don't send a certificate."] [1311 1 "// clientSessionCacheKey returns a key used to cache sessionTickets that could"] [1312 1 "// be used to resume previously negotiated TLS sessions with a server."] [1323 1 "// hostnameInSNI converts name into an appropriate hostname for SNI."] [1324 1 "// Literal IP addresses and absolute FQDNs are not permitted as SNI values."] [1325 1 "// See RFC 6066, Section 3."]] :go/pos {:name [5 9] :package [5 1]} :go/semis [[52 21] [125 59] [264 45] [289 80] [296 49] [307 55] [326 41] [436 76] [526 87] [586 53] [589 59] [596 31] [599 35] [602 49] [610 66] [615 49] [618 25] [622 31] [625 31] [628 49] 